~~
Keyword Modifier Edit Blocks

This test validates that keyword modifiers via .edit syntax work.
When a custom .end attribute is set on a write modifier, the modified
version uses that end string instead of the default newline.

  let Writef write.edit { .end: "" }

The PascalCase name distinguishes keyword modifier bindings from
regular variables. Invocations like `Writef "text"` use the custom
end string, while default `write "text"` continues to use "\n".
~~

let Writef write.edit { .end: "" }

Writef "hello "
write "world"

~ Expected Terminal Output: hello world
